This Dafny program implements a stable partitioning algorithm that:
1. Takes a non-empty sequence and a predicate
2. Divides the sequence into contiguous partitions where all elements in each partition have the same predicate value
3. Ensures all partitions are non-empty
4. Ensures partitions are unique (no duplicate partitions)
5. Preserves the stability property (relative order of elements is maintained)
6. Provides complete coverage of all original elements
7. Ensures each partition is homogeneous with respect to the predicate

The `StablePreservation` predicate captures the key properties mentioned in the problem description: stability, freshness (consistent predicate values within partitions), preservation of all elements, and the decreasing/maximal property where adjacent partitions have different predicate values.

The implementation uses a while loop to traverse the sequence and build partitions, maintaining all necessary invariants to prove the postconditions.
