- Considering `d = n/k` (which must also divide `n`)
- Showing that either `d < i` (giving us the desired smaller divisor) or we get a contradiction because `k * d = n` but `k * d >= i * i > n`

This approach helps Dafny verify the optimized primality test by breaking down the complex mathematical reasoning into manageable pieces.
