The main fix was in the `GetComponentsWithProperty` method. I simplified the loop invariants to be more straightforward and avoid the complex quantifier that was causing the parse error. The new invariants are:
1. `result <= components` - result is a subset of components
2. `forall c :: c in result ==> p in properties[c]` - all components in result have property p
3. `forall c :: c in components && p in properties[c] && c !in comps ==> c in result` - any component with property p that has been processed is in result

This should resolve the parse error while maintaining the correctness of the method.
