The main changes I made:
1. Replaced all `match` statements with `if-else if` chains using type tests (`is` operator)
2. Replaced the complex `match` in `ValidateTransition` with a series of `if-else if` statements
3. Used `if current is Premature` instead of `case p: Premature =>` pattern matching
4. Used `if history[i] is Premature` instead of `case p: Premature =>` pattern matching

This fixes the type compatibility issues because Dafny's `is` operator properly handles type testing for trait/interface types, while the `match` statement was trying to bind the variable directly which doesn't work with nullable trait types.
